file session-logs/date/README-index-20260906.md two rows an auto-merge seated out of order, swapped back
file construction/ITINERARY.md the git nib alone, read from the command; there was no room for an entry
obs THE SEND, recorded after it was over, which is why this follow-up exists (rule 5 of remember-git-nib, seated upstream this same hour). Five rebases, four of them pre-emptive on fetch rather than on a push refusal; the fleet landed 13 commits under this round. Scoped roster pass against the full-green basis fce04fe9da: 98 run, 96 green, 0 red, 31 skipped by scope, run_verdict=ok. Landed fb58822647 on xy then gp405, both remotes matching, tree clean.
obs AND THE ROUND'S OWN LESSON, stated plainly: five of the things I built this round were already built better by someone else by the time I looked up. Fetching earlier would have saved most of it. The tree's law handled every collision correctly and without loss -- the spine renumbered, the fold tool refused, the scan refused mid-rebase -- so nothing broke; what it cost was hours of work that had to be thrown away by hand, one file at a time.
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the card has 34 bytes free and no room for the next ship's line; folding it is a judgment about which accounts are finished, and that judgment is yours rather than a loop's.
